---
/** Terms of service for using the website. Not a contract for locksmith work —
 *  that is agreed with the customer before each job. */
import LegalPage from '@/components/LegalPage.astro';
import { business } from '@/data/business';
const updated = 'October 4, 2026';
---
<LegalPage title="Terms of Service" path="terms" updated={updated}
  description="The terms for using the Nico & Vito Locksmith website and requesting a quote through it.">

  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of nicovitolocksmith.com, run by {business.legalName} ("Nico &amp; Vito",
    "we", "us"). By using the site you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information on this site</h2>
  <p>
    The site gives general information about our locksmith services. Prices, arrival times and
    descriptions are guides, not guarantees: every job is different, and the price for your job is the
    one we agree with you before the work starts.
  </p>

  <h2>Requesting service</h2>
  <p>
    Sending the quote form, calling or texting us is a request for a quote. It does not create a contract.
    Any work is agreed directly between you and us. Before opening a lock or making a key, we may ask for
    identification and proof that you live at the address or own the vehicle.
  </p>
  <p>Please give accurate details and only request work on property you are entitled to have opened or changed.</p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    Do not misuse the site: no false or abusive submissions, no attempts to interfere with how it works,
    and no automated collection of its content.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The text, photographs and logo on this site belong to us and may not be copied or reused without our
    permission. Reviews and photos shown from our Google Business Profile come from Google and are shown
    as published there.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>The site links to services such as Google Maps. We are not responsible for the content or practices of those sites.</p>

  <h2>No warranty for the website</h2>
  <p>
    The website is provided "as is". We work to keep it accurate and available, but we do not promise it
    will always be error-free or online.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses arising from your use of the website
    itself. This does not limit any rights you have for work we carry out, which are governed by what we
    agree with you for that job and by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or call {business.phoneDisplay}.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
